think Opened on an orphaned --hot roster pass holding the lock, parent exited, 26 minutes old. Resolved every candidate through /proc/<pid>/cwd before signalling -- and pgrep -f standing_equipment_run matched my OWN claude process, since the baton text contains that string. Named pid, verified command line and tree, TERM, trap released the lock.
think Cold pass closed run_verdict=guard_red on seed_link alone, tree_moved=no, 190-odd guards otherwise green.
think %532's own scan named the remaining gap and called the cure the disease: a sampled desk "costs a judgment -- what value proves this gate? -- and then a fourth hand-written enumeration to hold the answer, which is the very shape %532 booked." The answer is to stop looking for a place to keep the list. The desk keeps its own.
think The marker goes in the SAME six-line head band the run-contract already uses, so one band answers every question the scan asks of a desk. Precedent: two markers already live there.
think Measured before written -- every one of the 46 desks run through tools/g/glow_run.rish with the values it now declares, 46 of 46 GREEN, so the ceilings fall onto a measurement rather than a hope.
obs The control caught my own fault before it shipped: the two-file awk idiom NR==FNR answers yes for EVERY record of the second file when the first is empty, so a room where no desk declares a sample consumed its whole selection as map entries and ran nothing -- while every printed count still read right. A clean room is the commonest room there is. The map is read in BEGIN now.
obs Both ceilings now stand at zero, so neither can be proven by dropping one lower. Each refusal leg raises its SIBLING's ceiling, because a silent runner trips both gates at once and the later verdict was overwriting the earlier one -- the bare leg was proving its sibling's refusal while naming its own.
obs Two witness pens moved from a pwd-derived /tmp name into this tree's own gitignored .lap/, which is the baton's newer clause and a stronger guarantee than the arithmetic it replaces.
obs %532 is repaired and the ledger cannot say so: the pin stands at 40,904 of 40,960 with rows_that_fit=0, so a deadlocked pin now blocks a REPAIR RECORD on an OPEN row, not only a new red. Three ships named the pin today; this is the fourth, and it is a different consequence.
obs Against myself, three times. The awk fault above was the first. The second: I read the cold pass's red list MID-RUN and reported one red where the closed pass named three -- seed_link, stash_record, and standing_equipment cascading off it. A list read before a pass closes is not a reading. The third: I applied the shelf-link repoint DURING the hot pass, which then refused tree_moved=yes, correctly; the pass was re-run on a still tree.
obs My shelf carried its elder block's links verbatim, so from one directory down they pointed at construction/archive/archive/. tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh computed the repair and applied exactly that -- the tree has a tool for this and my hand did not need to guess.
obs My own parked lap, measured rather than applied. stash@{0} holds a GREEN glow_literal_law rung -- does Glow accept a leading zero in a decimal literal, a language custody question -- beside a crushed_index edit whose diff now runs BACKWARD against the tree, because DIFFUSER landed the same repair since. Applying the stash whole would revert a peer's landed work, which is exactly the hazard REDS %636 booked. Restore the rung alone, on its own lap.
obs A red I cannot close, surfaced rather than routed around: seed_link RED, unbooked -- README.md links context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md, a room template-manifest.bron withholds. Both cures are somebody else's: allow the page (a privacy boundary, Keaton's word) or name it in prose (Petrichor's front door). The ratchet also rose 848 -> 850.
